	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Search listening TCP ports and their processes via the `portreaper` keyword. Filter by process name, port, or PID.

* ↩ Copy PID to the clipboard.
* ⌘↩ Send SIGTERM and reopen the list.
* ⌥↩ Send SIGKILL and reopen the list.
* → Open Universal Actions for the selected PID.

The list refreshes every second. Force killing a process can cause data loss. Processes owned by another user may not be stoppable.
</string>
